   "design": "Fixed rules in the time system list only the mismatches between clock records and the schedule, instead of reading every record. Employees request leave and overtime in the self-service app, so paper forms drop to exceptions. Approved hours export from the time system to payroll, instead of being typed again, and the time system's reports replace the attendance spreadsheet. Checking presence, talking with employees, entering corrections and approving timesheets stay with the postmaster.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Clock records, paper forms, spreadsheets and payroll were kept apart.",
   "enabler_now": "Time systems with exception rules, self-service leave and payroll export.",
   "still_hard": "Disputed hours that need a conversation.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing when a late arrival is a sign of trouble at home.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less checking and retyping; people judgement stays.",
   "reach": [
