   "design": "Employees enter availability in the scheduling app. The scheduling tool proposes a schedule from forecast volume, availability and the working-time and labour agreement rules as fixed constraints, with no model and no scoring of people. The postmaster adjusts it in the tool, instead of building it in a spreadsheet and typing it in. The tool flags rule breaks and publishes the schedule to staff. Talking with supervisors and staff, adjusting, deciding exceptions and handling swaps stay with the postmaster.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Schedules were built in spreadsheets and typed into the system.",
   "enabler_now": "Scheduling tools with rule constraints and self-service availability.",
   "still_hard": "Peaks no forecast foresaw.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing who can cover a hard shift without burning out.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
